                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Mark Wilks, Baptist preacher see Jewson, Jacobin City. His sermon on the
                            stability of the French revolution was published in 1792 describing him
                            as a Norfolk farmer. A funeral sermon for him was preached on 14.2.1819
                            at St George's Chapel Norwich by his nephew Mark Wilks 1783-1855 who was
                            a pastor in Hants and Wilts 1805-13, preached at New Broad St, London
                            1813-1819 and then went to Paris from 1820-1843 </p>
